{"hits":{"hits":[{"id":"472193","metadata":{"authors":[{"full_name":"Olum, Ken D."}],"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"81","page_end":"3570","year":1998,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214495"},"page_start":"3567","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett."}],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"I investigate the relationship between faster-than-light travel and weak-energy-condition violation, i.e., negative energy densities. In a general spacetime it is difficult to define faster-than-light travel, and I give an example of a metric which appears to allow superluminal travel, but in fact is just flat space. To avoid such difficulties, I propose a definition of superluminal travel which requires that the path to be traveled reach a destination surface at an earlier time than any neighboring path. With this definition (and assuming the generic condition) I prove that superluminal travel requires weak-energy-condition violation.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":472193,"titles":[{"title":"Superluminal travel requires negative energies"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Superluminal travel requires negative energies."},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Superluminal travel requires negative energies"}]},"created":"1998-06-24T00:00:00+00:00","updated":"2023-03-07T04:59:23.437005+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/472193?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/472193?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/472193?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/472193?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/472193?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/472193?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A472193"}}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Agr-qc%2F9805003&size=1&page=1&fields=titles,abstracts